      "arabicLemma": "انما فسر بذلك دفعا لما ربما يتوهم",
      "english": "The division into simple and compound is not being applied to every object called a “sign” or to the entire earlier sixfold classification. It applies specifically to a *conventionally assigned expression*. Without that restriction some nonverbal signs, such as mere gestures and inscriptions taken under another respect, would be incorrectly forced into the simple/compound lexical division. The expression assigned a meaning for syntactic combination is likewise not the object of the present classification unless that assigned meaning is considered.",
