      "english": "The original Aristotelian definition of a compound was commonly stated as an expression whose part indicates a part of its meaning. Later writers added that this indication must be **intended**, because a multiword expression such as “ʿAbd Allāh” may be used as a single proper name without intending its components separately to signify a servant and God. The logician's attention to semantic unity explains why this case differs from a grammatical division based on word count alone.",
