      "english": "A report is a complete expression **of a kind capable of truth or falsehood**, not one whose actual truth and falsity are both genuinely open once every fact has been determined. “The whole is greater than the part” is necessarily true, and “the part is greater than the whole” necessarily false, but both are reports because their predicative form can be evaluated for agreement or disagreement with reality. The criterion abstracts from the particular fact and considers the statement as an assertion.",
