      "arabicLemma": "قوله في الدار وخمسة عشر",
      "english": "Two nonrestrictive examples illustrate different reasons. In “in the house,” the particle *fī* indicates a specific relation rather than a generic absolute item which the following noun could narrow; “the house” supplies its relational endpoint. In “fifteen,” the word “five” may have a more general application by itself, but combining it with “ten” does not restrict that first term in the manner of an adjective modifying a noun; it forms a composite numeral. These cases also vary as to whether the second expression determines a sense of the first, whether the first is a particle or noun, and whether it governs the second.",
